The lesson map
Color channels are the main component of a color image. Therefore, we need to learn how to separate those color channels. This helps us understand different color intensities in the image and allows us to create mono-colored images.

What are color channels?
A color image consists of three color channels—blue, green, and red. We merge these three color channels to create color images. OpenCV allows us to split an image into respective color channels. Additionally, it allows us to merge the color channels to form a color image.

Split color channels
To split color channels, we use the cv2.split() method of the OpenCV library.


